<section data-aud-show="none" class="section is-light"><div class="container"><div class="section_header is-tight"><h2 class="heading-h2">FAQ</h2></div><div class="faq accordion"><div class="w-dyn-list"><div role="list" class="faq_list w-dyn-items"><div role="listitem" class="w-dyn-item"><div class="accordion_item"><div class="accordion_trigger"><div class="heading-h3">What can B2Bware do that AI alone cannot?</div><svg fill="none" viewBox="0 0 16 16" height="16" width="16" class="accordion_icon accordion_icon"><path stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-width="2" stroke="currentColor" d="M3.333 5.667 8 10.333l4.667-4.666"></path></svg></div><div class="accordion_content"><div class="faq_answer w-richtext"><p>AI needs a hand - and that is exactly what we give it.</p><p>Large models are powerful at drafting, classifying and suggesting. They still lack your commerce context: ERP rules, customer contracts, EU hosting constraints and the day-to-day reality of running a shop. B2Bware and the SyncSpider team supply that context - including through MCP - so AI assists inside a platform we operate for you.</p><p>You get a European commerce platform with ERP integration, hosting in the EU, updates and human support. AI helps you move faster; it does not replace the team that runs your stack.</p></div></div></div></div><div role="listitem" class="w-dyn-item"><div class="accordion_item"><div class="accordion_trigger"><div class="heading-h3">Who is B2Bware for - B2B, B2C, or both?</div><svg fill="none" viewBox="0 0 16 16" height="16" width="16" class="accordion_icon accordion_icon"><path stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-width="2" stroke="currentColor" d="M3.333 5.667 8 10.333l4.667-4.666"></path></svg></div><div class="accordion_content"><div class="faq_answer w-richtext"><p>Both. B2Bware is the European commerce platform for B2B and B2C - shop, customer portal, search, AI, sales channels and ERP integration in one system.</p><p>Wholesalers, manufacturers, distributors and retailers use it when they want to sell the way their customers buy, without stitching plugins or US-only stacks together. One shop, every channel - so your team can focus on selling, not administering tools.</p></div></div></div></div><div role="listitem" class="w-dyn-item"><div class="accordion_item"><div class="accordion_trigger"><div class="heading-h3">Does my ERP stay the source of truth?</div><svg fill="none" viewBox="0 0 16 16" height="16" width="16" class="accordion_icon accordion_icon"><path stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-width="2" stroke="currentColor" d="M3.333 5.667 8 10.333l4.667-4.666"></path></svg></div><div class="accordion_content"><div class="faq_answer w-richtext"><p>Yes. Your ERP stays at the center.</p><p>Prices, stock and orders sync automatically - no retyping, no reconciling between shop and back office. B2Bware is built around ERP integration, not around replacing the system you already trust. You do not have to change your processes; the platform adapts to how you already work.</p></div></div></div></div><div role="listitem" class="w-dyn-item"><div class="accordion_item"><div class="accordion_trigger"><div class="heading-h3">Is B2Bware GDPR-compliant and hosted in the EU?</div><svg fill="none" viewBox="0 0 16 16" height="16" width="16" class="accordion_icon accordion_icon"><path stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-width="2" stroke="currentColor" d="M3.333 5.667 8 10.333l4.667-4.666"></path></svg></div><div class="accordion_content"><div class="faq_answer w-richtext"><p>Yes - 100% EU by design.</p><p>Your shop, portal and data are hosted in the EU. AI processing stays in the EU as well, with no transfer to third countries. GDPR compliance is built in, not bolted on, and a data processing agreement is included.</p><p>B2Bware is built and operated in Europe by SyncSpider - Made in the EU, hosted in the EU - so you get legal certainty, contacts in your time zone and no dependency on US corporations for your most sensitive business data.</p></div></div></div></div><div role="listitem" class="w-dyn-item"><div class="accordion_item"><div class="accordion_trigger"><div class="heading-h3">Do I only pay for the modules I use?</div><svg fill="none" viewBox="0 0 16 16" height="16" width="16" class="accordion_icon accordion_icon"><path stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-width="2" stroke="currentColor" d="M3.333 5.667 8 10.333l4.667-4.666"></path></svg></div><div class="accordion_content"><div class="faq_answer w-richtext"><p>Yes. B2Bware is modular on purpose.</p><p>Shop, portal, search, AI, loyalty, social and channels live in one system - and you only pay for the modules you actually use. No plugin chaos, no stack of separate invoices for every add-on.</p><p>Exact packaging depends on your channels and ERP setup. Start a free trial or book a demo and we map the modules that fit your business - without forcing features you do not need.</p></div></div></div></div><div role="listitem" class="w-dyn-item"><div class="accordion_item"><div class="accordion_trigger"><div class="heading-h3">Should I start with a free trial or book a demo?</div><svg fill="none" viewBox="0 0 16 16" height="16" width="16" class="accordion_icon accordion_icon"><path stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-width="2" stroke="currentColor" d="M3.333 5.667 8 10.333l4.667-4.666"></path></svg></div><div class="accordion_content"><div class="faq_answer w-richtext"><p>Use the path that matches how you buy.</p><p><strong>Start a free trial</strong> when you want to explore the platform yourself - navigate, click through flows and see how B2Bware feels day to day.</p><p><strong>Book a demo</strong> when you want a guided walkthrough with your ERP, customer types and channels in mind. We show the fit, answer hard questions and outline next steps with people who run commerce platforms for a living.</p><p>Many teams do both: a short demo to align, then a trial to validate with their own team.</p></div></div></div></div><div role="listitem" class="w-dyn-item"><div class="accordion_item"><div class="accordion_trigger"><div class="heading-h3">Do you work with agencies and partners?</div><svg fill="none" viewBox="0 0 16 16" height="16" width="16" class="accordion_icon accordion_icon"><path stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-width="2" stroke="currentColor" d="M3.333 5.667 8 10.333l4.667-4.666"></path></svg></div><div class="accordion_content"><div class="faq_answer w-richtext"><p>Yes. Agencies, integrators and resellers are a core part of how B2Bware reaches the market.</p><p>Through the SyncSpider partner program you can refer customers or resell under your own name, with a partner portal for leads, deals, learning and commissions. We back partners with second-level support so you can stay close to your clients while we run the platform.</p><p>If you already advise manufacturers or wholesalers on commerce and ERP, partnering means you keep the relationship - and your customers get a European stack that stays maintainable.</p></div></div></div></div><div role="listitem" class="w-dyn-item"><div class="accordion_item"><div class="accordion_trigger"><div class="heading-h3">How does B2Bware integrate with my systems?</div><svg fill="none" viewBox="0 0 16 16" height="16" width="16" class="accordion_icon accordion_icon"><path stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-width="2" stroke="currentColor" d="M3.333 5.667 8 10.333l4.667-4.666"></path></svg></div><div class="accordion_content"><div class="faq_answer w-richtext"><p>ERP integration sits at the core - and the platform connects across 400+ integrations for the systems around it.</p><p>That means prices, stock and orders stay in sync with your ERP or PIM, while shop, portal and channels share one European stack instead of one-off project glue. You avoid expensive custom projects every time a channel or tool changes.</p><p>Bring your current landscape to a demo; we map what connects out of the box and where a tailored sync still makes sense.</p></div></div></div></div><div role="listitem" class="w-dyn-item"><div class="accordion_item"><div class="accordion_trigger"><div class="heading-h3">Why not plugins or a US SaaS stack?</div><svg fill="none" viewBox="0 0 16 16" height="16" width="16" class="accordion_icon accordion_icon"><path stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-width="2" stroke="currentColor" d="M3.333 5.667 8 10.333l4.667-4.666"></path></svg></div><div class="accordion_content"><div class="faq_answer w-richtext"><p>Because those stacks make you administer systems instead of sell.</p><p>Plugin shops bring slow load times, brittle updates, security gaps and hosting you still own. US SaaS often means ongoing app fees, data outside the EU and serious B2B features locked behind expensive plans.</p><p>B2Bware is the opposite: one central European platform we run, update and secure for you - hosting and security in the EU included, PageSpeed-focused without plugin bloat, ERP at the core. You keep selling. We keep the platform running.</p></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></section>